KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ run time: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
could not be evaluated
static assertion failed
^warning: ignoring
--
With libc++ (18 and Xcode 26) the constant evaluator cannot evaluate
`std::string_view{"32"} == "32"': operator== passes the views by value to
compare(), which calls char_traits<char>::compare(data(), __sv.data(),
__rlen) on a view whose value holds its pointer as the string literal
itself.  The comparisons of literals and constexpr arrays pass.
